                "file_text": "# Enhanced Spark Consumer Monitor\n\nA Python-based solution for reading Spark streaming checkpoint offsets from S3 and committing them to Amazon MSK (Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka) topics.\n\n## Overview\n\nThis project provides an automated way to:\n- Read Spark streaming checkpoint data from S3 storage\n- Parse offset information from checkpoint files\n- Commit offset data to MSK Kafka topics\n- Support multiple checkpoint folders and topics\n- Deploy and run on Amazon MWAA (Managed Workflows for Apache Airflow) 2.10.13\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nEnhancedSparkConsumerMonitor/\n├── dags/                   # Airflow DAG files\n├── plugins/                # Custom Airflow plugins and modules\n├── requirements/           # Python dependencies\n│   └── requirements.txt\n├── docs/                   # Documentation\n├── test/                   # Test scripts and data\n└── README.md              # This file\n```\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Multi-source Support**: Handle multiple Spark streaming checkpoint folders\n- **Multi-topic Commit**: Commit offsets to multiple Kafka topics\n- **MWAA Compatible**: Designed for Amazon MWAA 2.10.13\n- **Configuration Management**: Uses Airflow Variables for environment settings\n- **Error Handling**: Comprehensive error handling and logging\n- **Scalable**: Efficient processing of large checkpoint datasets\n\n## Technical Specifications\n\n- **Target Platform**: Amazon MWAA 2.10.13\n- **Python Version**: Python 3.x\n- **Key Dependencies**: kafka-python, boto3\n- **Configuration**: Airflow Variables for MSK broker strings and S3 paths\n\n## Quick Start\n\n1. Configure Airflow Variables for MSK broker strings\n2. Deploy to MWAA environment\n3. Schedule or trigger the DAG\n\nFor detailed setup and usage instructions, see the documentation in the `docs/` folder.",
                "command": "create"
              },
