        "ToolUse": {
          "message_id": "03c98ac2-326c-464b-9c06-8afb4f8ef1a2",
          "content": "",
          "tool_uses": [
            {
              "id": "tooluse_QhUS4AuQQguR46l6Da9V5Q",
              "name": "fs_write",
              "orig_name": "fs_write",
              "args": {
                "summary": "Add behavior explanation for checkpoint-based mapping",
                "path": "/Users/zhwenhao/qchatlog/EnhancedSparkConsumerMonitor/docs/airflow_variables_config.md",
                "new_str": "## Behavior\n\n### Consumer Group Resolution Priority:\n1. **Checkpoint-based mapping** (`checkpoint_consumer_group_mapping`): Maps S3 checkpoint paths to consumer groups\n2. **Topic-based mapping** (`kafka_consumer_group_mapping`): Maps topics to consumer groups  \n3. **Default fallback** (`kafka_consumer_group`): Single consumer group for all topics\n\n### Multiple Consumer Group Support:\n- **Primary**: Uses `checkpoint_consumer_group_mapping` for path-specific consumer groups\n- **Secondary**: Uses `kafka_consumer_group_mapping` to assign specific consumer groups to topics\n- **Fallback**: If neither mapping provided, uses `kafka_consumer_group` for all topics\n- **Validation**: System validates all consumer groups can connect to Kafka\n- **Isolation**: Each consumer group maintains independent offset tracking\n\n### Advanced Scenario Support:\n- **Same Topic, Different Apps**: Multiple Spark applications can process the same topic with different consumer groups\n- **Path-based Resolution**: Consumer groups are determined by checkpoint source path\n- **Conflict Resolution**: If same topic appears in multiple checkpoints, latest checkpoint wins\n- **Flexible Configuration**: Mix of checkpoint-based and topic-based mappings\n\n### Benefits:\n- **Application Isolation**: Different Spark applications maintain separate offset tracking\n- **Parallel Processing**: Multiple consumer groups can process same topics independently\n- **Flexible Configuration**: Supports complex multi-application scenarios\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Works with existing single consumer group setups",
                "old_str": "## Behavior\n\n### Multiple Consumer Group Support:\n- **Primary**: Uses `kafka_consumer_group_mapping` to assign specific consumer groups to topics\n- **Fallback**: If mapping not provided, uses `kafka_consumer_group` for all topics\n- **Validation**: System validates all consumer groups can connect to Kafka\n- **Isolation**: Each consumer group maintains independent offset tracking\n\n### Benefits:\n- **Topic Isolation**: Different applications can track offsets independently\n- **Parallel Processing**: Multiple consumer groups can process same topics\n- **Flexible Configuration**: Mix of shared and dedicated consumer groups\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Works with existing single consumer group setups",
                "command": "str_replace"
              },
              "orig_args": {
                "summary": "Add behavior explanation for checkpoint-based mapping",
                "path": "/Users/zhwenhao/qchatlog/EnhancedSparkConsumerMonitor/docs/airflow_variables_config.md",
                "new_str": "## Behavior\n\n### Consumer Group Resolution Priority:\n1. **Checkpoint-based mapping** (`checkpoint_consumer_group_mapping`): Maps S3 checkpoint paths to consumer groups\n2. **Topic-based mapping** (`kafka_consumer_group_mapping`): Maps topics to consumer groups  \n3. **Default fallback** (`kafka_consumer_group`): Single consumer group for all topics\n\n### Multiple Consumer Group Support:\n- **Primary**: Uses `checkpoint_consumer_group_mapping` for path-specific consumer groups\n- **Secondary**: Uses `kafka_consumer_group_mapping` to assign specific consumer groups to topics\n- **Fallback**: If neither mapping provided, uses `kafka_consumer_group` for all topics\n- **Validation**: System validates all consumer groups can connect to Kafka\n- **Isolation**: Each consumer group maintains independent offset tracking\n\n### Advanced Scenario Support:\n- **Same Topic, Different Apps**: Multiple Spark applications can process the same topic with different consumer groups\n- **Path-based Resolution**: Consumer groups are determined by checkpoint source path\n- **Conflict Resolution**: If same topic appears in multiple checkpoints, latest checkpoint wins\n- **Flexible Configuration**: Mix of checkpoint-based and topic-based mappings\n\n### Benefits:\n- **Application Isolation**: Different Spark applications maintain separate offset tracking\n- **Parallel Processing**: Multiple consumer groups can process same topics independently\n- **Flexible Configuration**: Supports complex multi-application scenarios\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Works with existing single consumer group setups",
                "old_str": "## Behavior\n\n### Multiple Consumer Group Support:\n- **Primary**: Uses `kafka_consumer_group_mapping` to assign specific consumer groups to topics\n- **Fallback**: If mapping not provided, uses `kafka_consumer_group` for all topics\n- **Validation**: System validates all consumer groups can connect to Kafka\n- **Isolation**: Each consumer group maintains independent offset tracking\n\n### Benefits:\n- **Topic Isolation**: Different applications can track offsets independently\n- **Parallel Processing**: Multiple consumer groups can process same topics\n- **Flexible Configuration**: Mix of shared and dedicated consumer groups\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Works with existing single consumer group setups",
                "command": "str_replace"
