    "> based on current deployment, could you provide the varible configation sample to me?",
    "Based on the current deployment, here are the Airflow Variable configuration samples you'll need to set up:\n[Tool uses: fs_write]",
    "I've created a comprehensive Airflow Variables configuration guide in `docs/airflow_variables_config.md`. Here's the quick setup for your specific environment:\n\n## **Minimal Required Configuration:**\n\n```bash\n# Required variables for your setup\nairflow variables set msk_broker_string \"b-1.zhwenhaomsk.88je25.c5.kafka.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:9092,b-2.zhwenhaomsk.88je25.c5.kafka.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:9092\"\n\nairflow variables set s3_checkpoint_paths '[\"s3://zhwenhaodatalake/checkpoints/stockprice/offsets/\"]'\n\nairflow variables set kafka_topics '[\"stockprice\"]'\n```\n\n## **Key Points:**\n\n1. **MSK Broker String**: Your exact broker addresses (comma-separated)\n2. **S3 Paths**: JSON array format recommended, supports multiple checkpoint folders\n3. **Kafka Topics**: JSON array format, should match topics in your checkpoint data\n4. **Optional**: Consumer group defaults to `spark-checkpoint-monitor`\n5. **Optional**: AWS region defaults to `us-east-1`\n\n## **For MWAA Environment Variables (Alternative):**\n```bash\nAIRFLOW_VAR_MSK_BROKER_STRING=\"b-1.zhwenhaomsk.88je25.c5.kafka.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:9092,b-2.zhwenhaomsk.88je25.c5.kafka.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:9092\"\nAIRFLOW_VAR_S3_CHECKPOINT_PATHS='[\"s3://zhwenhaodatalake/checkpoints/stockprice/offsets/\"]'\nAIRFLOW_VAR_KAFKA_TOPICS='[\"stockprice\"]'\n```\n\nThe DAG includes automatic validation that will check all these variables and fail gracefully with clear error messages if anything is missing or misconfigured.\n\nWould you like me to proceed with creating the testing scripts, or would you prefer to set up these variables and test the current deployment first?\n[Tool uses: none]",
    "> based on cuttent deployment, do we support multiple consumer group?",
    "Looking at the current deployment, **no, we do not support multiple consumer groups**. Here's the current implementation:\n\n## Current Consumer Group Implementation:\n\n1. **Single Consumer Group**: The system uses one consumer group for all offset commits\n2. **Configuration**: Set via Airflow Variable `kafka_consumer_group` (defaults to `spark-checkpoint-monitor`)\n3. **Usage**: All topics use the same consumer group when committing offsets\n\n## Current Code Structure:\n```python\n# In config_manager.py\ndef get_consumer_group(self) -> str:\n    return self.get_variable(\n        key='kafka_consumer_group',\n        default_value='spark-checkpoint-monitor'\n    )\n\n# In kafka_offset_committer.py\ndef __init__(self, bootstrap_servers: str, consumer_group: str = 'spark-checkpoint-monitor'):\n    self.consumer_group = consumer_group  # Single group for all operations\n```\n\n## Would you like me to add multiple consumer group support?\n\nIf you need multiple consumer groups, I can enhance the system to support:\n\n1. **Topic-specific consumer groups**: Different consumer groups for different topics\n2. **Checkpoint-path-specific groups**: Different consumer groups for different S3 checkpoint folders\n3. **Configurable mapping**: Airflow Variables to define topic → consumer group mappings\n\n**Example enhanced configuration:**\n```json\n{\n  \"stockprice\": \"stock-consumer-group\",\n  \"userdata\": \"user-consumer-group\", \n  \"transactions\": \"transaction-consumer-group\"\n}\n```\n\nShould I implement multiple consumer group support, or is the single consumer group sufficient for your use case?\n[Tool uses: none]",
    "> I need to support multiple consumer group, and consumer group name need to be defined in varible",
    "I'll enhance the system to support multiple consumer groups with variable-based configuration. Let me update the relevant modules:\n[Tool uses: fs_write]",
